---

## 🧠 What changed

| File | Before | After |
|------|--------|-------|
| **AudioRecorderHelper** | Did not exist | New class that uses `AudioRecord` to capture microphone input and writes a proper WAV file. |
| **MainViewModel** | `startRecording` only created an empty placeholder file | Now launches a coroutine that actually records audio via `AudioRecorderHelper`. `stopRecording` waits for the recording to finish, then hands the valid WAV file to `WhisperBridge`. |

Now when you press the **Record button**, the app will:
1. Start listening to the microphone.
2. When you press Stop, it writes a fully formed WAV file.
3. Passes that file to the native Whisper stub (which will return a test string until you replace it with the real whisper.cpp).

---

## ⚠️ Next step: real Whisper transcription

The **JNI stub** (`whisper_jni.cpp`) still only returns a placeholder string like:

```
[Whisper STUB] Would process: /data/...temp_audio.wav | model=tiny | lang=English | mode=transcribe
```

To get actual speech-to-text, you need to:

1. Clone [whisper.cpp](https://github.com/ggerganov/whisper.cpp) into `app/src/main/cpp/whisper/`
2. Uncomment the CMake lines in `CMakeLists.txt`
3. Replace the stub functions with calls to `whisper_full()`
4. Place a GGML model (e.g., `ggml-tiny.bin`) in `assets/models/`

Full instructions are in `app/src/main/cpp/INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md`.

---

Now the recording side is real — **you can capture audio**. The transcription will become real as soon as you plug in whisper.cpp.

I'll integrate whisper.cpp into your project. Since I can’t run `git clone` directly on your machine, I’ll provide a **setup script** that does the cloning automatically, plus I’ll fully rewrite the JNI code to use the real Whisper API and update the build files so the native library compiles correctly. After you run the script, just rebuild the project and the real transcription will work.

---

## 1. Setup script – clones whisper.cpp into your project

<file path="app/src/main/cpp/clone_whisper.ps1">
```powershell
# PowerShell script to clone whisper.cpp into the correct location
Set-Location $PSScriptRoot
Write-Host "Cloning whisper.cpp into $pwd\whisper ..."
git clone https://github.com/ggerganov/whisper.cpp.git whisper
Write-Host "Done. The whisper.cpp source code is now in app/src/main/cpp/whisper."
Write-Host "Next: place a GGML model file (e.g., ggml-tiny.bin) in app/src/main/assets/models/ and build the project."
```
</file>

**Before the next step, run this script** from `app/src/main/cpp/` to clone the repository. Then continue.

---

## 2. Updated CMakeLists.txt – builds whisper.cpp and links it

<file path="app/src/main/cpp/CMakeLists.txt">
```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.18.1)
project("whisper_jni")

# Include whisper.cpp as a subdirectory
add_subdirectory(whisper)

# Our shared library
add_library(
    whisper_jni
    SHARED
    whisper_jni.cpp
)

target_include_directories(whisper_jni PRIVATE
    ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}
    ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/whisper
)

# Link against whisper and its dependencies
target_link_libraries(whisper_jni
    whisper
    ${log-lib}
)

target_compile_options(whisper_jni PRIVATE
    -std=c++17
    -O2
    -Wall
)

# If whisper.cpp needs additional flags, they are handled in its own CMakeLists.txt
```
</file>

---

## 3. Real WhisperBridge.kt – passes model file path instead of directory

<file path="app/src/main/java/com/noteflowai/app/whisper/WhisperBridge.kt">
```kotlin
package com.noteflowai.app.whisper

/**
 * JNI bridge to the native Whisper C++ library.
 * All heavy AI processing runs on-device via this interface.
 */
class WhisperBridge {

    private var nativePtr: Long = 0

    companion object {
        init {
            System.loadLibrary("whisper_jni")
        }
    }

    /**
     * Initialize the Whisper engine with a model file.
     * @param modelFilePath Absolute path to the GGML model file (e.g., .bin)
     * @return true if initialization succeeded
     */
    external fun initialize(modelFilePath: String): Boolean

    /**
     * Transcribe or translate an audio file.
     * @param audioFilePath Path to WAV file (16kHz, mono, 16-bit PCM)
     * @param language Source language (e.g., "en", "zh", "ja", "ko", "id")
     * @param transcribe True for transcription, false for translation to English
     * @return The transcribed/translated text
     */
    external fun transcribe(
        audioFilePath: String,
        language: String,
        transcribe: Boolean
    ): String

    /**
     * Release native resources.
     */
    external fun release()
}
```
</file>

