## 🧾 Final checks

- ✅ Model loading now shows **clear error messages** if the `.bin` file is missing.
- ✅ The Record screen **blocks interaction** and clearly tells you what’s wrong.
- ✅ Changing model in Settings automatically **re‑copies the new file** and re‑initializes.
- ✅ WAV loader now handles **non‑standard chunks** (metadata etc.) — more robust.
- ✅ Permission denial shows a toast and avoids crashing.

Now the only remaining requirement is to place the actual GGML model file in `assets/models/`. If you haven’t already, download e.g. `ggml-tiny.bin` from [here](https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp/resolve/main/ggml-tiny.bin) and put it in `app/src/main/assets/models/`. Then rebuild — transcription will work.

We need to decouple recording from automatic transcription, so you can record audio files first and transcribe them later on demand. The C++/JNI side remains unchanged; only the Kotlin UI and ViewModel are restructured.

